1 Also used in pyomo.
\(\mathbf{x}\quad\) the vector of variables \((x_1,\ldots,x_n)^\top \in \mathbb{ R}^n\), also called unknowns or parameters.
\(f\quad\) the objective, or cost function to minimize or maximize.
\(\mathbf{c}\quad\) the vector function of \(m\) constraints \((c_1(\mathbf{x}), \ldots, c_m(\mathbf{x}) )\) that the unknowns must satisfy. Then, the optimization problem becomes \[\begin{equation}
  \min_{\mathbf{x}\in \mathbb{ R}^{n}}f(\mathbf{x})\qquad\mathrm{subject}\,\,\mathrm{to}\,\begin{array}{cc}
      \left\{ \begin{array}{cc}
          c_{i}(\mathbf{x})=0, & \quad i\in\mathcal{E},\\
          c_{i}(\mathbf{x})\geq0, & \quad i\in\mathcal{I},
      \end{array}\right.\end{array}\label{eq:pbopt}
\end{equation} \tag{1}\]







2 The computation time increases with \(N\) as \(\exp (cN)\) and becomes prohibitively expensive as the number of variables, \(N,\) increases.3  https://www.ibm.com/analytics/cplex-optimizer and https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CPLEX
